[99.978428, "o", "# MLService Deployment Fix\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nThe service was failing with \"No module named 'tokenizers'\" when run with `python -m mlservice` from within the `/home/user/mlservice` directory.\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\nWhen running `python -m mlservice` from inside the mlservice directory itself, Python's module resolution cannot properly import the mlservice package. The package needs to be run from its parent directory (`/home/user`).\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nUse the provided `start_service.sh` script instead of running `python -m mlservice` directly.\r\n\r\n### For Production Deployment\r\nReplace:\r\n"]
[99.978479, "o", "```bash\r\ncd /home/user/mlservice\r\nsource .venv/bin/activate\r\npython -m mlservice\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith:\r\n```bash\r\ncd /home/user/mlservice\r\n./start_service.sh\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr simply:\r\n```bash\r\n/home/user/mlservice/start_service.sh\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script handles venv activation and ensures the service runs from the correct directory.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\nThe service now successfully imports tokenizers and all other dependencies.\r\n"]
[99.978648, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[99.978686, "o", "user@017c47f8dc78:~/mlservice$ "]
